    "answer": {
      "short": "Refund of \\$2940.67.",
      "worked": "The taxable income is in the \\$180 001 and over bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Excess} &= 278639-180000 \\\\\n\\text{Excess} &= 98639 \\\\\n\\text{Income tax} &= 51667+0.45\\times98639 \\\\\n\\text{Income tax} &= \\$96054.55 \\\\\n\\text{Medicare levy} &= 0.02\\times278639 \\\\\n\\text{Medicare levy} &= \\$5572.78 \\\\\n\\text{Total tax} &= 96054.55+5572.78 \\\\\n\\text{Total tax} &= \\$101627.33 \\\\\n\\text{PAYG}-\\text{Total tax} &= 104568-101627.33 \\\\\n\\text{PAYG}-\\text{Total tax} &= \\$2940.67\n\\end{align*}$$\nPAYG payments exceed total tax, so Anand receives a refund of \\$2940.67.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
